				<wikidot:authorName>Sniblet</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3938764</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>&quot;<em>D-9031 complies. The camera is located so the photograph cannot be seen.</em>&quot;<br /> It seems out of character for the foundation to use such minimal protection against such a threat, or, for that matter, against anything whatsoever.<br /> If 9031 wanted to prove that he had removed them as he did (it's a good thing that the first two were blank), or if he had learned the power of the photographs somehow (GOI meddling would do it), he could have just rotated the photo, and thus, murdered the research team.<br /> It didn't happen, but that doesn't mean it couldn't have. Tsk tsk, doctor Dan.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
